# What the knowledge graph should not index. .gitignore syntax, and everything
# git already ignores is skipped without being listed here — this file is only
# for the things that survive that filter and still do not belong in the graph.

# `npm run build:mcp` bundles src/core/ into here. It is generated, and it is
# git-ignored, but graphify still picks it up — and because it is a copy of code
# that is already indexed, every symbol in src/core/ lands in the graph twice.
# The duplicates are what make it worth listing: they split the edges for a
# function between two nodes and make `graphify explain` ambiguous.
mcp-server/core.js

# Binary media. Indexing these needs the optional image/video extras and buys
# nothing for navigating the codebase — the demo GIFs are README illustrations
# and the icons are build artefacts of scripts/build-icons.mjs.
*.gif
*.png
*.jpg
*.ico
public/fonts/
